    # Single evaluation: HE_0's locked-in optimized hardening parameters,
    # but with DamageParameter1 pushed to near-zero (not just ThresholdDamage
    # raised) so D_dot = d1*<...>^d2*eqps_dot stays ~0 regardless of local
    # plastic strain -- the first attempt (d1=3.5, ThresholdDamage=0.999)
    # was NOT actually damage-free: D still crossed 0.999 during extreme
    # necking strain localization late in the run, producing a real bond-
    # failure event at ~16-17% strain (confirmed by the sharp drop + violent
    # oscillation in the resulting curve). This mirrors how Stage 1 runs
    # disable Johnson-Cook damage elsewhere in this project (D1=5.0, an
    # unreachable fracture strain) rather than relying on ThresholdDamage
    # alone. Not an optimization -- a one-off reference run for the
